WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.246 --> 00:00:14.909
they were doing nothing wrong, Laurie and Jo felt like two very naughty children.

2
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:20.653
Sitting up straight, hands folded in their laps, neither young one dared to utter a sound.

3
00:00:21.614 --> 00:00:24.836
"You say you are too ill to have your lessons with Mr.

4
00:00:24.956 --> 00:00:26.017
Brookes," Mr.

5
00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:26.817
Laurence began.

6
00:00:26.837 --> 00:00:32.604
"My tutor," Laurie whispered under his breath to Jo.

7
00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:34.245
"Did you say something, boy?"

8
00:00:34.765 --> 00:00:37.187
Mr. Laurence stood menacingly in front of Laurie.

9
00:00:37.207 --> 00:00:45.831
"No, sir," squeaked Laurie, "I mean, I was telling Jo, who's our neighbor you know that lovely family

10
00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:52.575
with all those girls, and Jo, here, being the second eldest well, I was telling her who Brookes

11
00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:53.655
was, I mean, Mr.

12
00:00:53.675 --> 00:00:54.116
Brookes, sir."

13
00:00:55.136 --> 00:00:58.678
Jo felt a giggle in her throat as poor Laurie rambled on.

14
00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:02.240
"What's so funny, girl?"

15
00:01:02.972 --> 00:01:05.153
Mr. Laurence moved over to where Jo sat.

16
00:01:06.614 --> 00:01:09.636
At that moment, the whole situation seemed oddly hilarious.

17
00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:14.619
Holding back the laughter that bubbled inside was causing Jo physical pain.

18
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.961
She could no longer do it.

19
00:01:16.981 --> 00:01:24.585
"Oh, I'm dreadfully sorry, sir," roared Jo, wiping the tears from her eyes.

20
00:01:25.966 --> 00:01:28.948
Both Laurie and his grandfather were shocked at her outburst.

21
00:01:30.684 --> 00:01:38.811
"Well, Laurie looks horribly sick and that ugly doll he's holding Jo's voice cracked but she continued, "As

22
00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:42.434
for me, I should be ladylike and not laugh out loud.

23
00:01:43.175 --> 00:01:47.538
And you Jo stopped herself before she did further damage.

24
00:01:48.419 --> 00:01:53.163
But to her astonishment, the old man looked at her with a twinkle in his eye and said,

25
00:01:53.183 --> 00:01:55.465
"Please continue.

26
00:01:56.066 --> 00:01:58.488
I'd like to know what is so funny about me."

27
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:06.612
Ignoring Laurie's kicks from under the table, Jo cleared her throat and went on: "Well, you're like a

28
00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:12.615
schoolmaster who has just caught his two most naughty pupils doing something terrible but he doesn't know what.

29
00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:21.360
So you're frowning and grunting and trying so hard to look upset but but Jo gasped for breath,

30
00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.562
"to me, sir, it's absolutely comical."

31
00:02:26.503 --> 00:02:29.537
Still chuckling, Jo stood up and gathered her things.

32
00:02:29.557 --> 00:02:34.960
"But I understand that I was completely out of line.

33
00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:41.624
My sisters tell me that I am so boorish, that's what the youngest, Amy, says, and I'm sure

34
00:02:41.664 --> 00:02:46.947
the others agree, though Beth, being so sweet and gentle, would never tell me that to my face,

35
00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.989
but I do cause so much embarrassment to our family.

36
00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:55.632
So before I do any more damage, I had better leave," Jo babbled.

37
00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.362
She caught a glimpse of Laurie bowing his head lower and his shoulders quivering.

38
00:03:00.382 --> 00:03:04.585
"That boy is laughing at me," she said to herself.

39
00:03:05.425 --> 00:03:11.148
Resisting the temptation to give Laurie a playful punch, Jo, instead, took a deep breath, faced the old

40
00:03:11.188 --> 00:03:15.331
man and said, "Sir, may I speak freely one last time?"

41
00:03:15.351 --> 00:03:18.612
"You've been saying whatever you like until now.

42
00:03:19.433 --> 00:03:20.133
Why stop?"

43
00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.575
Mr. Laurence said in a teasing voice.

44
00:03:22.595 --> 00:03:27.069
"Well, in my opinion, sir, I think Laurie is a splendid boy.

45
00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:33.113
And what he really needs to feel better is some warm love and lots and lots of laughter,"

46
00:03:33.533 --> 00:03:34.293
said Dr.

47
00:03:34.354 --> 00:03:36.095
Jo. Mr.

48
00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.535
Laurence was a shrewd man.

49
00:03:38.496 --> 00:03:41.938
He had already noticed how different Laurie seemed when he was with Jo.

50
00:03:42.759 --> 00:03:45.200
The change in his grandson was a pleasant one.

51
00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:51.684
"Then maybe you'd better stay and make sure he gets well," was the old man's surprising remark.

52
00:03:52.756 --> 00:03:55.357
He smiled warmly at Jo and then at his grandson.

53
00:03:57.138 --> 00:03:58.639
Later on she described Mr.

54
00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:05.641
Laurence's transformation to her sisters this way: "It was as if another person took over his body and

55
00:04:05.681 --> 00:04:08.303
he suddenly turned into the kindest man in the world."

56
00:04:09.083 --> 00:04:12.564
From that moment on, Laurie became the daily visitor to the March home.

57
00:04:13.425 --> 00:04:15.466
During the day he had his lessons with Mr.

58
00:04:15.486 --> 00:04:18.967
Brookes, a handsome intelligent young man employed by Mr.

59
00:04:18.987 --> 00:04:21.048
Laurence to help with his grandson's studies.

60
00:04:22.184 --> 00:04:27.489
Left with no choice after Laurie refused to attend boarding school, his grandfather finally agreed to let him

61
00:04:27.549 --> 00:04:31.372
receive home-schooling until he went off to university the following year.

62
00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:35.636
Even during his lessons, Laurie had one eye on the time.

63
00:04:36.657 --> 00:04:42.582
As the hands of the antique grandfather clock in the library inched toward four, Laurie's ears strained for

64
00:04:42.642 --> 00:04:46.365
the now-familiar sounds of his neighbors returning from their day's activities.

65
00:04:47.847 --> 00:04:49.068
Amy would come home first.

66
00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:55.304
Laurie recognized how she slammed the door in her impatience to shut out any memory of the school

67
00:04:55.344 --> 00:04:59.827
day. Then she would call out in a childish shrill, "Hannah!

68
00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.067
Can I have a snack?

69
00:05:01.388 --> 00:05:02.608
I'm so famished!"

70
00:05:03.609 --> 00:05:07.932
Meg and Jo came home around the same time but their entrance was completely different.

71
00:05:09.173 --> 00:05:14.396
Laurie never knew when Meg returned home exactly because he would not hear her going into the house

72
00:05:14.476 --> 00:05:14.997
like Amy.

73
00:05:16.398 --> 00:05:21.621
But from where he sat, he could see Meg walk into the kitchen, say hello to Hannah, put

74
00:05:21.681 --> 00:05:24.122
on her apron, and help the housekeeper prepare dinner.

75
00:05:25.203 --> 00:05:27.964
Thinking about his friend Jo brought a smile to Laurie's lips.

76
00:05:29.305 --> 00:05:34.448
Jo, knowing that Laurie would be watching out for her return, would make all kinds of noises to

77
00:05:34.528 --> 00:05:35.969
let him know she was home.

78
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.912
One time, she started to hum a funny song as she walked up the path to their door.

79
00:05:41.772 --> 00:05:44.974
Laurie had burst out into laughter, alarming and troubling Mr.

80
00:05:44.994 --> 00:05:48.796
Brookes, who was in the middle of explaining a rather dismal subject.

81
00:05:49.892 --> 00:05:51.333
Then, on another occasion, Mr.

82
00:05:51.373 --> 00:05:57.355
Brookes was explaining a tricky mathematical problem on the blackboard when he was interrupted by a strange barking

83
00:05:57.395 --> 00:06:00.717
noise. Looking out the window, Mr.

84
00:06:00.737 --> 00:06:05.319
Brookes could not see any canine in the area, but he did happen to catch a glimpse of

85
00:06:05.359 --> 00:06:08.480
a girl hastily shutting the entrance door over at the March home.

86
00:06:09.841 --> 00:06:15.183
Of the four girls, Beth stayed home all day but Laurie could not make out any sounds that

87
00:06:15.243 --> 00:06:16.624
alerted him to where she was.

88
00:06:18.192 --> 00:06:22.714
Once, he thought he heard very soft singing, but Laurie could not be sure if it was Beth,

89
00:06:23.094 --> 00:06:25.956
who he knew loved to sing, or if he had imagined it.

90
00:06:25.976 --> 00:06:32.258
"As your attention has already left the lesson and moved on to the affairs in the other house,"

91
00:06:32.939 --> 00:06:36.620
Mr. Brookes declared, closing his book, "you may be excused now."

92
00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:41.422
Giving him a mock salute, Laurie sprang up, and leaped out of the library.

93
00:06:42.623 --> 00:06:44.704
Nothing was ever boring at the Marches' home.

94
00:06:45.652 --> 00:06:50.115
The girls always had plenty to keep themselves occupied and there was never a shortage of things to

95
00:06:50.155 --> 00:06:50.655
talk about.

96
00:06:51.555 --> 00:06:56.038
On this particular evening, the conversation ranged from spiders to dinner invitations.

97
00:06:57.279 --> 00:07:00.821
"Grandfather would love for all of you to come for dinner tomorrow," Laurie said.

98
00:07:01.741 --> 00:07:02.341
Although Mr.

99
00:07:02.362 --> 00:07:08.545
Laurence had extended the invitation on several occasions, Mother was delaying accepting it until Beth felt comfortable enough

100
00:07:08.585 --> 00:07:11.166
around Laurie to venture over to the unfamiliar house.

101
00:07:11.186 --> 00:07:15.509
"That's very kind of him," Beth replied in her soft way.

102
00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.912
Laurie and Jo stopped playing cards to stare at her.

103
00:07:18.932 --> 00:07:21.954
"Does that mean you'd like to come to my house?"

104
00:07:22.394 --> 00:07:22.875
asked Laurie.

105
00:07:23.635 --> 00:07:29.699
Beth smiled shyly at Laurie and said: "To me, you're more than a neighbor, Laurie, you're our dear

106
00:07:29.779 --> 00:07:30.200
friend."
